WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.695
HKDSE 2026, Paper 1, Question 6. Topic: Compound Inequalities. This is the full worked solution in English.

2
00:00:11.115 --> 00:00:22.788
Consider the compound inequality 3x minus 4 is less than 5 is less than or equal to 2 minus 7x over 6 … (times). (a) Solve (times).

3
00:00:22.948 --> 00:00:27.442
(b) Write down the greatest integer satisfying (times).

4
00:00:27.862 --> 00:00:32.967
STEP 1 — split into two inequalities.

5
00:00:33.127 --> 00:00:39.756
3x minus 4 is less than 5 and 5 is less than or equal to 2 minus 7x over 6.

6
00:00:40.176 --> 00:00:45.175
STEP 2 — solve the first inequality.

7
00:00:45.335 --> 00:00:51.881
3x minus 4 is less than 5 which gives 3x is less than 9 which gives x is less than 3.

8
00:00:52.301 --> 00:00:57.371
STEP 3 — solve the second inequality.

9
00:00:57.531 --> 00:01:04.417
Key rule: Reversing the Inequality Sign. a minus kb (k is greater than 0).

10
00:01:04.577 --> 00:01:14.991
Dividing 28 is less than or equal to minus 7x by minus 7 gives minus 4 is greater than or equal to x, i.e. x is less than or equal to minus 4.

11
00:01:15.151 --> 00:01:19.964
Multiply through by 6 (positive, so the sign is unchanged).

12
00:01:20.124 --> 00:01:30.043
30 is less than or equal to 2 minus 7x which gives 28 is less than or equal to minus 7x Divide by minus 7 and reverse the inequality sign.

13
00:01:30.203 --> 00:01:36.136
minus 4 is greater than or equal to x which gives x is less than or equal to minus 4.

14
00:01:36.556 --> 00:01:41.519
STEP 4 — intersect the two ranges.

15
00:01:41.679 --> 00:01:51.808
Key rule: Intersection of Solution Sets. x is less than or equal to minus 4 and x is less than 3 which gives x is less than or equal to minus 4.

16
00:01:51.968 --> 00:02:01.333
The stricter upper bound x is less than or equal to minus 4 lies inside x is less than 3, so the overlap is x is less than or equal to minus 4.

17
00:02:01.493 --> 00:02:10.713
Both must hold: x is less than or equal to minus 4 and x is less than 3. The intersection is x is less than or equal to minus 4.

18
00:02:11.133 --> 00:02:15.153
Step 5. PART (b).

19
00:02:15.313 --> 00:02:27.331
The greatest integer satisfying x is less than or equal to minus 4 is minus 4 itself (since x equals minus 4 satisfies both 3(minus 4)-4 equals minus 16 is less than 5.

20
00:02:27.491 --> 00:02:33.590
and 5 is less than or equal to (2 plus 28) over 6 equals 5).

21
00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:40.344
So the answer is: (a) x is less than or equal to minus 4 (b) minus 4.

22
00:02:40.764 --> 00:02:49.689
That completes HKDSE 2026 Paper 1 Question 6. Every step shown here matches the worked solution on the page.
